%N A321733 Number of (0,1)-matrices with n ones, no zero rows or columns, and the same row sums as column sums.
%C A321733 Also the number of labeled digraphs with n arcs, loops allowed, no multiple arcs or isolated vertices, and equal indegree and outdegree at every vertex. - _Vladeta Jovovic_, Nov 13 2026
%H A321733 Vladeta Jovovic, <a href="/A321733/b321733.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..47</a>
%F A321733 Let B_j(x) = [z_1^0*...*z_j^0] (1 + x)^j*Product_{1 <= r < s <= j} (1 + x*z_r/z_s)*(1 + x*z_s/z_r), with B_0(x) = 1. Then a(n) = [x^n] Sum_{k=0}^n Sum_{j=0}^k (-1)^(k-j)*binomial(k,j)*B_j(x), where [z_1^0*...*z_j^0] extracts the terms in which every z_i has exponent 0. - _Vladeta Jovovic_, Nov 13 2026
